#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for the content interface, which lets producer snaps "
"share code, data, libraries, and sockets with consumer snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:8
msgid "content interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `content` interface allows sharing code and data from a slot on a "
"_producer_ snap to one or more plugs on _consumer_ snaps. It's often used to "
"share common themes and icons from a producer snap, for example, to many "
"snapped applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Sharing happens at the filesystem level, which means anything that can be "
"expressed as a file can be shared. This includes executables, libraries and "
"data files, but also sockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:14
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"The [Yaru MATE Icons](https://github.com/ubuntu-mate/icon-theme-yaru-mate-"
"snap) snap is a good producer snap example, letting other applications "
"access the wonderful MATE icon theme. But there are many other producer "
"snaps too, including several for [GTK Common Themes](https://snapcraft.io/"
"gtk-common-themes), [KDE Frameworks](https://snapcraft.io/kf6-core24) for "
"better application integration with the desktop, and [Mesa](https://"
"github.com/canonical/mesa-2404) for a graphical libraries stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:18
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"**Auto-connect**: no, unless connecting to snaps from the same publisher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:22
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:23
msgid ""
"**source (slot)**: allows multiple directories to be exposed separately "
"rather than grouped together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:24
msgid "**read (slot)**: _read-only_ paths to be exposed to a consuming snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"**write (slot)**: _read and write_ paths to be exposed to a consuming snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:26
msgid "**target (plug)**: path in consuming snap to find producer snap's files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:27
msgid "**default-provider (plug)**: name of preferred producer snap (`<SNAP>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"**content (slot and plug)**: an arbitrary identifier for content type. "
"Defaults to either local slot name or local plug name for slot/plug "
"definitions respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"**interface (slot and plug)**: snapd interface name (must be `interface: "
"content`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:31
msgid "Sharing content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"By default, when multiple directories are shared from a producer snap, or "
"when multiple slots are connected to a single plug, the shared content is "
"merged under the `target` path of the consuming path's plug definition. This "
"behaviour can be modified with the `source` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"Read, write and target should start with either ``$SNAP``, ``$SNAP_DATA`` or "
"``$SNAP_COMMON`` to refer to the designated directory. See {ref}`Environment "
"variables <reference-development-environment-variables>` for details on "
"where these point to on the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:37
msgid ""
"Paths declared in a slot's `source` attribute can also reference "
"`$SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME`, but only within a path that starts with `$SNAP_DATA` "
"or `$SNAP_COMMON`. This is useful for sharing a separate, per-instance "
"directory with consumers of a {ref}`parallel-installed <interfaces-parallel-"
"installs>` producer snap. See the {ref}`Parallel installed content providers "
"section <interfaces-content-interface-parallel-installs>` below. Requires "
"_snapd_ 2.79+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"The _content identifier_ specified by the consuming snap (plug) must match "
"the _content_ attribute of the producer snap (slot)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"At a very basic level, the content interface enables one directory, file or "
"socket to appear in a place where another snap can access it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"Each example below involve two snaps: the first provides some content (using "
"a content _slot_) while the second consumes that content (using a content "
"_plug_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"In all of the cases we see a small set of attributes defined on the "
"particular interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:46
msgid ""
"the producer declares which path can be read, using either the `read` "
"attribute for read-only, or the `write` attribute for both read and write "
"permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:47
msgid ""
"the consumer uses the `target` attribute to define where the content should "
"become available at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"both the producer and consumer use an arbitrary `content` attribute to "
"describe the content. This attribute must match on both sides for the "
"connection to happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:50
msgid "Using <code>source</code>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:50
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:137
msgid "<code>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:50
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:137
msgid "</code>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:52
msgid ""
"The `source` attribute presents one or more sub-directories, shared from a "
"slot to a plug, **beneath** the plug's `target` path. Adding the `source` "
"attribute ensures that sub-directories, shared from one or more producer "
"snaps, are presented separately to the consumer snap beneath its `target` "
"path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:54
msgid ""
"When multiple slots are connected to the same plug _and_ they share "
"directories with the same name, those directories are given unique names "
"with the following pattern:  `<directory>`, `<directory>-2`, "
"`<directory>-3`, `<directory>-x`. The first connection keeps the original "
"directory name from the slot; subsequent connections with the same name get "
"the suffixed form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:56
msgid ""
"With the following example, directories from the producer snap are shared in "
"corresponding directories beneath the _consumer_ snap's `target` path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:58
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:107
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:141
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:178
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:203
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:236
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:298
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:319
msgid "**producer/snapcraft.yaml**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:60
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  <slot_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: my-binaries\n"
"    source:\n"
"      read:\n"
"        - $SNAP/bin   # binaries to share\n"
"        - $SNAP/libs  # libraries to share\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:71
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:118
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:151
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:188
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:213
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:248
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:329
msgid "**consumer/snapcraft.yaml**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:72
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  <plug_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: my-binaries\n"
"    target: $SNAP/connected-content\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:80
msgid ""
"Using the above configuration, the consumer snap could implement a part to "
"run an executable from the following path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:82
msgid "$SNAP/connected-content/bin/<executable-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:86
msgid "While the libraries are accessible at:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:88
msgid "$SNAP/connected-content/libs/<library-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:92
msgid ""
"When more than one slot, providing similarly named sources, is connected to "
"the same plug, the plug directory for the new connection will be incremented:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:94
msgid "$SNAP/connected-content/bin-2/<executable-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:98
msgid "Directory names are preserved after a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:101
msgid "Parallel installed content providers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:103
msgid "_Requires snapd 2.79+._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:105
msgid ""
"When a slot's `source` attribute declares paths starting with `$SNAP_DATA` "
"or `$SNAP_COMMON` and with `$SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME` as the final path element, "
"it allows a consumer snap to get a separate directory for each instance of "
"the {ref}`parallel-installed <interfaces-parallel-installs>` producer snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:108
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  <slot_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: assets\n"
"    source:\n"
"      read:\n"
"        - $SNAP_DATA/assets/$SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:119
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  <plug_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: assets\n"
"    target: $SNAP_DATA/assets\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:127
msgid ""
"If multiple instances of producer snap such as `my-producer`, `my-"
"producer_inst1` and `my-producer_inst2` are all connected to the consumer's "
"plug, the consumer sees each producer's content under its own instance name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:129
msgid ""
"$SNAP_DATA/assets/my-producer/...\n"
"$SNAP_DATA/assets/my-producer_inst1/...\n"
"$SNAP_DATA/assets/my-producer_inst2/...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:135
msgid ""
"Since `$SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME` is only known at content provider snap "
"installation time, it can only be used when sharing data from writable "
"locations, such as `$SNAP_DATA` or `$SNAP_COMMON`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:137
msgid "Using the <code>read</code> and <code>write</code> attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:139
msgid ""
"Without the `source` attribute, content from the producer snap is mounted at "
"the **exact path** indicated in the consumer snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:142
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:179
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  <slot_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: my-binaries\n"
"    read:\n"
"      - $SNAP/bin\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:152
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:189
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  <plug_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: my-binaries\n"
"    target: $SNAP/usr/local/bin\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:160
msgid ""
"Using the above configuration, the consumer snap can access executables "
"using the following path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:162
msgid "$SNAP/usr/local/bin/<executable-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:166
msgid ""
"When more than one slot is connected to the same plug, the plug directory "
"for the new connection will be incremented using the same mechanism as with "
"the `source` attribute described above (`<directory>`, `<directory>-2`, "
"`<directory>-3`, `<directory>-x`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:168
msgid ""
"It is recommended to only expose a single `read` path using this "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:170
msgid "Read-only content sharing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:172
msgid ""
"Read-only content sharing is ideal for executables, libraries and files "
"related to global graphical themes or images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:174
msgid "Sharing an executable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:176
msgid ""
"When the following two interfaces are connected, the *consumer* snap can "
"invoke executables from `$SNAP/usr/local/bin`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:197
msgid ""
"The directory can be added to `PATH` in the wrapper script, if desired, and "
"the directory can also be inspected by any applications that wish to check "
"if the extra executables are available (they can then fail gracefully)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:199
msgid "Sharing a C-level library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:201
msgid ""
"A consumer snap can link to libraries shared by a producer snap, using the "
"`read`/`write` attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:204
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  old-libraries:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: lib0-1604\n"
"    read:\n"
"      - $SNAP/lib\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:214
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  old-libraries:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: lib0-1604\n"
"    target: $SNAP/extra-libs\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:222
msgid ""
"After connecting the interface, the *consumer* snap can link to libraries "
"from `$SNAP/extra-libs`. The directory can be added to `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` in "
"the wrapper script if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:224
msgid ""
"The value of the `content` attribute can be anything, but it is good "
"practice to follow the form `nameAPI-BUILDENV` to remind slot consumers of "
"the API level and build tools used. This naming convention is also "
"_required_ when sharing content between snap publishers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:226
msgid "In the above example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:227
msgid "`0` indicates API level 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:228
msgid ""
"`1604` denotes Ubuntu 16.04 LTS toolchain and libraries were used within the "
"build environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:230
msgid ""
"API and BUILDENV can be anything that is meaningful to the provider and "
"consumers. For example, the GNOME content snap uses `gnome-3-26-1604` to "
"denote the full GNOME 3.26 platform libraries and supporting files built on "
"Ubuntu 16.04 LTS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:232
msgid "Sharing icons or themes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:234
msgid ""
"A consumer snap can link to themes shared by a producer snap, which exposes "
"multiple directories using the `source` attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:237
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  icon-themes:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: icon-themes\n"
"    source:\n"
"      read:\n"
"        - $SNAP/share/icons/Yaru-MATE-dark\n"
"        - $SNAP/share/icons/Yaru-MATE-light\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:249
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  icon-themes:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: icon-themes\n"
"    target: $SNAP/themes\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:257
msgid ""
"After connecting the interface, the *consumer* snap can observe all themes "
"under `$SNAP/themes`, and the directories would be exposed as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:259
msgid ""
"$SNAP/themes/Yaru-MATE-dark\n"
"$SNAP/themes/Yaru-MATE-light\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:264
msgid "Content identifier obligations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:266
msgid ""
"The content identifier attribute identifies a mostly-immutable compatibility "
"contract (API/ABI or similar) between the snap providing the corresponding "
"content and the snaps consuming it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:268
msgid ""
"The providing snap must preserve backward compatibility for the content "
"provided under a given identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:270
msgid ""
"Equally, updates to consuming snaps cannot strongly depend on changes of the "
"identified content from updates to the providing snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:272
msgid ""
"There is no support in _snapd_ to synchronise updates between consuming and "
"providing snaps. Compatibility breaking changes need to happen under a "
"different content identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:274
msgid "Default provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:276
msgid ""
"The optional `default-provider` attribute can be used to set to the name of "
"a snap offering a corresponding content slot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:278
msgid "**consumer/snapcraft.yaml**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:279
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  lib0-1604:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: lib0-1604\n"
"    target: $SNAP/extra-libs\n"
"    default-provider: lib01604\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:288
msgid ""
"If the system does not contain a snap providing a matching slot, installing "
"a consumer snap with a default-provider will trigger the automatic "
"installation of the named provider snap.  If the named snap is already "
"installed, the absence of a matching slot will instead trigger an update of "
"the named provider snap. The plug and slot will be auto-connected assuming "
"the {ref}`auto-connection mechanism <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-"
"connection>` is configured properly for this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:290
msgid ""
"For example, a snap consuming the GNOME content snap for GNOME 3.26 can set "
"`default-provider` to `gnome-3-26-1604`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:292
msgid "Sharing writable data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:294
msgid ""
"Sharing writable data can be used to share data files, and _UNIX sockets_, "
"between a group of snaps. This allows for the creation of a simple form of "
"IPC between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:296
msgid "Sharing writable files (from _snapd 2.19.1_):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:299
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  <slot_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: writable-data\n"
"    write:\n"
"      - $SNAP_DATA\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:308
msgid "**consumer/snapcraft.yaml:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:309
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  <plug_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: writable-data\n"
"    target: $SNAP_DATA\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:317
msgid "Sharing UNIX sockets (from _snapd 2.19.1_):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:320
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  <slot_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: socket-directory\n"
"    write:\n"
"      - $SNAP_DATA\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:330
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  <plug_name>:\n"
"    interface: content\n"
"    content: socket-directory\n"
"    target: $SNAP_DATA\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:338
msgid ""
"When the two interfaces are connected the *consumer* snap can see the socket "
"in `$SNAP_DATA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:340
msgid "Technical details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:342
msgid ""
"The content interface is implemented via an interplay between two systems: "
"[AppArmor](https://wiki.ubuntu.com/AppArmor) and bind mounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:345
msgid ""
"By default, the AppArmor sandbox allows _writes_ to `$SNAP_DATA` and _reads_ "
"from `$SNAP` (see {ref}`Environment variables <reference-development-"
"environment-variables>` for details)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:347
msgid ""
"The content interface takes advantage of this feature to map data from other "
"locations to either `$SNAP` or `$SNAP_DATA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:349
msgid ""
"A bind mount is then created to link `$SNAP` in one snap (e.g. from `/snap/"
"my-snap/1234/content`) to an empty directory in the other snap  (e.g., to `/"
"snap/my-other-snap/4321/incoming-content`). Locations need to be selected "
"carefully because a bind mount could potentially permit mounts over "
"important locations, such as `$SNAP_DATA`, preventing access to a snap's own "
"writable space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:351
msgid ""
"The same can be done for particular files, if desired, but it requires a "
"pair of interfaces for each file and is more cumbersome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:353
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:355
msgid ""
"The previously mentioned [Yaru MATE Icons](https://snapcraft.io/icon-theme-"
"yaru-mate) snap is a good example of how this interface can be used to share "
"media with other snaps. Its snapcraft.yaml can be found here: [https://"
"github.com/ubuntu-mate/icon-theme-yaru-mate-snap/blob/main/snap/"
"snapcraft.yaml](https://github.com/ubuntu-mate/icon-theme-yaru-mate-snap/"
"blob/main/snap/snapcraft.yaml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/content-interface.md:358
msgid ""
"The source code for this interface is in the *snapd* repository: <https://"
"github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/content.go>"
msgstr ""
